properties.description:
The `/g/&lt;graph_id&gt;/` router — the transport half of per-session design selection, and the thing that gave Registry::discover a caller outside its own tests. A hand-written hyper/tower Service because this crate deliberately does not take axum. Holds one StreamableHttpService per design, opened ON DEMAND, with a per-id OnceCell so concurrent first requests for one design collapse into a single open rather than racing, and, since 2026-09-27, a lifecycle:
- a design idle past --registry-idle is closed;
- at --registry-max-open the least recently used idle design is closed to make room;
- only when every slot is serving a request is the newcomer refused, with 503 and Retry-After, never 404;
- closing ends the design's sessions;
- a reopen waits until the previous copy has released its store.
Until then, a cap refused past its limit and nothing was ever closed. Isolation holds by construction: the only way to name a design is the id segment, it goes straight to Registry::attach, and each design has its own session manager so a session id minted under one prefix is unknown under another.
